    "body": "Thanks! I started reviewing this, but then noticed that the spec already has a good example for this, at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#optional-tags\n\nIf you want to fix a different bug, my review might still be helpful for things to keep in mind, so here it is (don't do these for this PR):\n- Add your name(s) to the ACKS section.\n- Wrap lines at 100 (maybe not the DOM trees, though?)\n- The DOM tree `<ul>` should not be in the `<pre>`. The prose in `<pre>` should also be moved out and be wrapped in `<p>`s.\n- Remove `<ref spec=ATOM>`s (and a stray `</p>` tag).\n- Typo reuslted.\n- Use lowercase element names in the DOM tree, like in https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/introduction.html#a-quick-introduction-to-html\n- Squash into one commit, and make the commit message\n  \n  ```\n  Add syntax examples for omitting tag rules\n  \n  Fixes https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=27319.\n  ```\n\nAlso if you make more PRs, it is probably a good idea to create a new branch in your fork.\n\nIf you can get https://github.com/whatwg/html-build running you can check the output and it tells you about some markup mistakes (in this case `</p>`).\n",
